<article class="env-definition" id="06U6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06U6">Definition <span data-tag="06U6">101.12.2</span>.</a> Let $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a morphism of algebraic stacks. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $f$ is <em>submersive</em><a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001722951" id="a0001722951-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> if the continuous map $|\mathcal{X}| \to |\mathcal{Y}|$ is submersive, see Topology, Definition <a href="/tag/0406" data-tag="0406">5.6.3</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $f$ is <em>universally submersive</em> if for every morphism of algebraic stacks $\mathcal{Y}' \to \mathcal{Y}$ the base change $\mathcal{Y}' \times _\mathcal {Y} \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}'$ is submersive. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>